# Chapter 7, part 5: the lists of files, TeX Font Association, the help
# viewer, the menu inside the Editor, Quit, the messages and the terminal and
# X11 versions.

.h2 Choosing a file or a directory from a list [str-browse]
.ix Listing of files
.ix File list
.ix Browse, files and directories
.ix Keypad + in panels
.ix F2, list of choices
.ix Printers, list
.ix Directory list
.ix Use this directory
A field that holds the name of a file, of a directory or of a printer can be
filled from a list.  Move to the field and press {k:Keypad +}, {k:Alt-+},
{k:+} or {k:F2}: the four keys do the same.  The plus key is taken by the list
on those fields, so a plus sign cannot be typed in them (the Caution in
{n:str-keys-panel}).  On any other field {k:F2} does nothing and the plus
sign is typed.
.table 20 10 20
Field | Shows | Files shown
Document Name | files | Names that end in {c:.doc}.
Help file | files | Names that end in {c:.hlp}.
Editor program | files | All files.
Working Directory | directories | None.
Initial Working Directory | directories | None.
Printer | printers | The queues of the system.
.end
The suffix is compared without regard to the case of letters.  Subdirectories
are always shown.
.h3 The list of files and directories [str-browse-list]
.ix List of files, keys
.ix Parent directory, list
The list is a box over the panel.  Its title is the directory that it shows
(when the name is longer than 56 characters, its last part with three dots
before it).  The entries are, in this order:
.table 22 38
Entry | Meaning
[Use this directory] | A list of directories only: take the directory that the
 | list shows.
../ | The directory above (not shown at the top of the tree).
NAME/ | A subdirectory: choose it to go into it.
NAME | A file with one of the suffixes of the table.
.end
The directories and the files are each sorted so that names that begin with a
capital letter come before the others.  Names
that begin with a point are shown.  A file or a directory that cannot be read as
a status (a broken link) is left out.
.table 19 41
Key | Effect
{k:Up} {k:Down} | Move the highlight one entry.
{k:Home} {k:End} | Go to the first or to the last entry.
{k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} | Move by a page of the box.
{k:Enter} | Choose the entry: a directory is entered and the list is drawn
 | again, a file or [Use this directory] ends the list.
{k:Esc} | Leave the list.  The field is not changed.
A letter or digit | The next entry that begins with it; in a list of twelve
 | entries or fewer it is chosen at once ({n:str-keys-list}).
.end
The list starts in the directory that the Working Directory field of the panel
holds; when the panel has no such field (Setup), or the field is not a
directory, in the directory of the name already in the field, and otherwise
in the current directory.  When the name of a directory cannot be read the
notice "Cannot read the directory" (title Directory) is shown.
.h3 What the choice does to the panel [str-browse-effect]
.ix Document Name, chosen from the list
.ix Working Directory, changed by the list
.table 22 38
Field | After the choice
A file, with a Working Directory field in the panel | The Working Directory
 | field is set to the directory of the list and the file field to the file
 | name alone.
A file, with no such field (Setup) | The field holds the whole path.
A directory | The field holds the directory.
.end
.h2 TeX Font Association [str-fonts]
.ix TeX Font Association
.ix Fonts, list for printing
.ix Font list, TeX
.ix LaTeX package of a font
.ix CTAN
.ix Install Now
.ix Lato
A font of a document is a number from 1 to 20 (Headline, Text and
Header/Footer, then Font 4 to Font 20; {n:format-typeface}).  The
entry TeX Font Association of the menu keeps, for each number, the LaTeX font
that it stands for: the package that selects the font, the options of the
package and the family.  A font is a package of LaTeX or, for the fonts that
every LaTeX has, nothing.  The list belongs to the user, not to a document.
.h3 The list of the twenty fonts [str-fonts-list]
.ix Font list, keys
.ix not installed
.pic pictures/str-fonts-list.png 5.2 The list of fonts: TeX Font Association.
The entry opens a menu titled TeX Font Association, with the instruction Press
Ins to Change a Font, and twenty lines.  A line shows, in columns, the number
of the font, its name (24 characters at most), its LaTeX package (15 at most;
(LaTeX default) for a name that has no package, and nothing when there is no
name) and the words "not installed" when the package is named and TeX cannot
find it.  The
keys are those of the menus of {x:str-keys-menu}: {k:Enter} or {k:Ins} opens the
panel of the highlighted font, {k:Esc} leaves the list, and a letter or digit
moves to the next line that begins with it (the lines begin with the number).
The highlight stays on the font that was used.
.h3 The panel of a font [str-fonts-panel]
.ix Font panel
.ix Font Number
.ix LaTeX Package
.ix Package Options
.ix Family, font
.ix CTAN Archive to Download
.ix Map File to Enable
.ix Installed, font
.ix Install Now (Yes or No)
.pic pictures/str-font-panel.png 5 The panel of a font.
The panel is titled Font N.  It has the keys of every panel of the Document
Manager ({n:str-keys-panel}); {k:Ins} accepts it and {k:Esc} leaves the font as
it was.
.table 20 10 20
Field | Default | Meaning
Font Number | the number | Dimmed (n/a).  The number of the font.
Name | per font | The name that panels show for the font.
LaTeX Package | per font | The package that selects the font.
Package Options | per font | The options of the package.
Family (roman, sans or mono) | per font | How the font is selected.
CTAN Archive to Download | empty | The archive for Install Now.
Map File to Enable | empty | The map file that Install Now enables.
Installed | Yes or No | Dimmed (n/a).  Whether TeX finds the package.
Install Now (Yes or No) | No | Yes downloads and installs the font.
.end
.rows 24 46
Name | Any text without a vertical bar, up to 47 characters.  The name is
 | what is shown in the lists of fonts of the Keycap Format panel and
 | of the Keycap marker ({n:markers}).
LaTeX Package | The name of a LaTeX package such as {c:mathpazo}, up to 47
 | characters; empty for the fonts that LaTeX has without a package (Computer
 | Modern).  Only letters, digits and the characters . _ - + = , are allowed.
Package Options | The options of the package, such as {c:scaled=0.92}, up to 63
 | characters, with the same characters.
Family | A choice: {c:roman}, {c:sans} or {c:mono}.  {k:Space} takes the next
 | one and goes round to the first after the last; {k:Left}, {k:Right} and
 | {k:F2} choose too.  The font is selected as the roman, sans serif or
 | typewriter family once the package is loaded.
CTAN Archive to Download | The name of the archive on CTAN, without its suffix,
 | for example {c:lato}: the file {c:lato.tds.zip} of the directory
 | {c:install/fonts}.  It may not hold a slash.  Same characters as above.
Map File to Enable | The map file of the font, such as {c:lato.map}; empty when
 | the font needs none.  Same characters as above.
Install Now | A choice, No or Yes.  {k:Space} changes it, as it does every field
 | that has a fixed set of values.  Yes installs the font when the panel is
 | accepted.  The field is always No when the panel opens.
.end
.h3 The values that a new user has [str-fonts-default]
.ix Font list, defaults
.ix Latin Modern, default font
.ix TeX Gyre
.ix psnfss
The list that comes with Strata names fonts that every TeX Live has, except
the last one.
.table 4 18 18 10
No | Name | Package | Family
1 | Latin Modern Sans | lmodern | sans
2 | Latin Modern Roman | lmodern | roman
3 | Latin Modern Roman | lmodern | roman
4 | Times | mathptmx | roman
5 | Helvetica | helvet, scaled=0.92 | sans
6 | Courier | courier | mono
7 | Palatino | mathpazo | roman
8 | Bookman | bookman | roman
9 | New Century Schoolbook | newcent | roman
10 | Avant Garde | avant | sans
11 | Zapf Chancery | chancery | roman
12 | Charter | charter | roman
13 | Utopia | utopia | roman
14 | TeX Gyre Termes | tgtermes | roman
15 | TeX Gyre Heros | tgheros | sans
16 | TeX Gyre Pagella | tgpagella | roman
17 | TeX Gyre Cursor | tgcursor | mono
18 | Computer Modern Roman | none | roman
19 | Lato | lato, default | sans
20 | not set | none | roman
.end
The outlines behind the names of the standard PostScript fonts (4 to 13) are the
free ones that TeX Live carries, not the fonts of the makers of those names.
Font 19, Lato, needs the download: its archive is {c:lato} and its map file
{c:lato.map}.  A font that is not set (20) shows no name.
.h3 What is saved, and when [str-fonts-save]
.ix Font list, file
.ix fonts, file of the user
.ix STRATA_HOME, fonts
.ix Install Now, programs
When a panel is accepted and all values are good, the font is changed and the
list is saved in the file {c:fonts} in the settings directory of the user
({c:.strata} in the home directory, or the directory that {c:STRATA_HOME}
names), the same directory as the file {c:config}
({n:appcfg}).  Leaving the list with {k:Esc} saves nothing more.  A font whose
entry in the file cannot be read has its default.
.table 31 29
Fault | Notice (title Font)
The family is not roman, sans or mono | The family is roman, sans or mono;
 | not saved
A bar in the name, or a character that is
 not allowed in the package, the options, | Only letters, digits and . _ - + = ,
 the archive or the map file | can be used for the package, options,
 | archive and map file; not saved
.end
Nothing is changed after one of these notices: the panel is not shown again, and
the list returns.  If the file cannot be written a notice titled Fonts gives the
reason, which is one of the messages of {x:format-messages-options} or
"Font N has a character that cannot be used (only letters, digits and . _ - +
= , are allowed)".  The change is then in effect until the program ends.
.h3 Install Now [str-fonts-install]
.ix Install Now, steps
.ix Font download
.ix curl, unzip, mktexlsr, updmap-user
Install Now makes a font that TeX does not have available for the user, without
any privilege and without touching the system.  While it works a box titled
Installing font names the step that runs: "Downloading NAME..." with the size
received so far, "Unpacking NAME...", "Making the file list of TeX
(mktexlsr)..." and "Enabling the map file MAP (updmap-user)...".  {k:Esc}
stops the download: the footer then shows "Installation cancelled", the partial
file is removed and nothing is installed.  The steps after the download are
short and cannot be stopped; the box shows "Please wait".  The font is fetched as an archive from CTAN
({c:https://mirrors.ctan.org/install/fonts/} followed by the name of the
archive and {c:.tds.zip}) and unpacked into the TeX directory of the user.  The
programs that do the work must be installed.
.if .STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release
.ix STRATA_CTAN_URL
For developers: the environment variable {c:STRATA_CTAN_URL} names another
directory that holds the archives, also a {c:file:} one.
.endif
.table 19 41
Program | Use
{c:curl} | Fetches the archive.
{c:unzip} | Unpacks it.
{c:kpsewhich}, mktexlsr | Find the TeX directory of the user and make TeX see the
 | new files (a TeX system).
updmap-user | Enables the map file, when the font has one.
.end
A good end shows a notice titled Installed with the text "Installed in
DIR".  The other ends show a notice titled Install failed.
.table 32 28
Text of the notice | Cause
This font has no archive to download | CTAN Archive to Download is empty.
The name of the archive or of the map file | A character that is not allowed,
 has a character that cannot be used | or a slash in the archive.
{c:kpsewhich} did not run (is TeX installed?) | TeX is not on the machine.
Cannot make a temporary directory | Strata cannot write in {c:TMPDIR}, or in
 {c:/tmp} when {c:TMPDIR} is not set.
The archive could not be downloaded from URL | No network, or the archive does
 | not exist.
The archive could not be unpacked | The unpacking failed.
updmap-user failed to enable the map file | The map file name is wrong.
.end
Installing a font does not change a document: the font that a number stands
for is only read when a document is printed or shown, and the list is only
read for the pictures of keycaps (the next section says where).
.h3 Where the list is used [str-fonts-use]
.ix Font list, use
.ix Keycap, font of
The list is read by the Editor for the legend of a keycap that is drawn as a
picture on the screen of the X11 version, and for the names that the Font field
of the Keycap Format panel and of the Keycap marker offers.  The Printer does
not read it: the pages of a Print and of a Preview are always set in Latin
Modern, in the family that the name of the font in the Typeface List gives
({n:print}, Fonts).  A font that the list shows is not installed is left out in
the picture of a keycap and the legend is set in the roman face.
.caution Changing a font here does not change what is printed.  To change the
  look of the printed page, change the names of the fonts in the Typeface List
  of the document ({n:format}).

.h2 The help viewer [str-help]
.ix Help viewer
.ix Help file
.ix F1, help
.ix Help topics
.ix Help Index
The help of the Document Manager is read from a help file and shown in a window
across the foot of the screen.  The help file is the one named by the setting
Help file of Setup; the places where it is looked for are in
{x:str-help-search}.  The window and its keys are described in {x:view-help};
this section tells what {k:F1} shows in the Document Manager.
.h3 Reaching the help [str-help-reach]
.ix F1, context
.ix Help, topic of a panel
{k:F1} on a menu or on a panel opens the window on the topic that fits it.
.table 29 31
Where {k:F1} is pressed | Topic
The main menu | The topic of the entry that is highlighted
Edit / Preview / Print Document | Edit / Preview / Print Document
Maintain Dictionaries | Maintain Dictionaries
Compare Document Versions | Compare Document Versions
The comparison report | Comparison Report
TeX Font Association | TeX Font Association
Setup | Setup
New File | Edit / Preview / Print Document
A dimmed field of Setup | A topic that says the setting is not used
A message in a box | The topic of the message, or of the box
.end
When the file has no topic for the place, the topic of the program is shown.
When no help file has been found, {k:F1} shows a notice titled Help that reports
this and reports how to name a help file; any key closes it.

.h2 The menu inside the Editor [str-inside]
.ix Editor, own menu
.ix Document Manager, inside the Editor
.ix Start of the Editor with no document
.ix Entry menu of the Editor
The Editor can be started with no document name.  The Editor then shows an
empty editing screen with a menu on it that has the title Document Manager and
the
four entries of the table.  It is not the program of this chapter: it has
no Setup panel and no list of fonts.  The usual way to start Strata
is the Document Manager, which starts the Editor on a document it has chosen.
.table 4 24 22
No | Entry | What it does
1 | Edit / Preview / Print Document | A list: Enter a file
 | | name, Choose from this directory, New document.
2 | Maintain Dictionaries | The panel of the personal word lists
 | | ({n:str-spell-words}).
3 | Compare Document Versions | The panel that compares two documents
 | | ({n:str-compare}).
4 | Quit | Ends the program with status 0.
.end
{k:Up}, {k:Down}, {k:Home}, {k:End}, {k:PgUp}, {k:PgDn}, {k:Enter} and the first
letter of an entry work as in a list ({n:str-keys-list}): a letter chooses at
once.  {k:Esc} shows the menu again.  Enter a file
name prompts for a name in one line (".doc" is added when it has no dot, and
the question "File does not exist. Create it?" is asked when it is not found);
Choose from this directory is the list of files of Retrieve ({n:file}); New
document is New of the File menu.  When a document is opened the menu goes away
and the editing screen is the one of the document.
.note To check the spelling of a document, open it and use Tools, Spell
  ({n:spell}).

.h2 Quit [str-quit]
.ix Quit
.ix Leaving the Document Manager
.ix Ending Strata
Quit ends the Document Manager.  There is no question and nothing is saved by
it (the settings are saved by Setup when it is accepted, the list of fonts when
a font is accepted).  The program ends with status 0.  No document is open at
that time, because each Editor ended before the menu came back.  The keys
that choose Quit are {k:Q}, which highlights it, and {k:Enter} or {k:Ins}, or
{k:End} and then one of them.  Only Quit ends the program: {k:Esc} on the
main menu, {k:Ctrl-Q} and the closing of the window of the X11 version leave
it on the screen ({n:str-keys-menu}).

.h2 Messages of the Document Manager [str-messages]
.ix Messages, Document Manager
.ix Error messages, Document Manager
.ix Notices, Document Manager
.ix Footer messages
The messages are of three kinds: the footer messages (one line in bold in the
last row of the screen, until the next key), the notices (a box that any key
closes) and the lines written on the standard error before the screen is
open.  Where a message belongs to a
section of this chapter the table says which.  The parts in capitals vary.
.h3 Footer messages [str-messages-footer]
.table 31 29
Text | Where and why
Enter a document name | Edit / Preview / Print Document: no document name.
Cannot find directory DIR | The Working Directory (or the directory part of
 | the name) does not exist.
Settings saved to PATH | Setup was accepted and written.
Installation cancelled | TeX Font Association, Install Now: {k:Esc} stopped the
 download.
A footer message that names the field and shows that it is not available in
 this version | A character is typed in a dimmed field
 (n/a): the Font Number and Installed fields of a font panel.
.end
.h3 Notices [str-messages-notices]
The title of the box is the first column.
.table 22 18 10
Title | Text | Section
Edit / Preview / Print Document | Cannot run the editor: PATH |
 {x:str-edit-end}
Edit / Preview / Print Document | The editor ended with status N |
 {x:str-edit-end}
Setup | The reasons in the table of {x:str-setup-accept} | {x:str-setup-accept}
Setup | Settings are in effect but could not be saved | {x:str-setup-accept}
Font | The family is roman, sans or mono; not saved | {x:str-fonts-save}
Font | Only letters, digits and . _ - + = , can be used ... | {x:str-fonts-save}
Fonts | The reason that the list could not be written | {x:str-fonts-save}
Installed | Installed in DIR | {x:str-fonts-install}
Install failed | The reasons of the table | {x:str-fonts-install}
Directory | Cannot read the directory | {x:str-browse-list}
Help | No help file was found | {x:str-help-reach}
.end
.h3 The standard error [str-messages-stderr]
.ix Standard error, Document Manager
.ix Usage text
These lines are written before the screen opens, and the program then ends.
.table 34 26
Text | When
A line that shows the program needs an interactive | There is no terminal, or
 terminal (or an X display with the X11 build) | in the X11 version no display.
 | Status 1.
The usage text, a few lines | The option {c:-h} or {c:--usage}.  Status 0.
Two lines: the name and the version, and the file format | The option
 {c:--version}.  Status 0.
.end
The exit statuses are in {x:str-exit}.

.h2 The terminal version and the X11 version [str-versions]
.ix Terminal and X11, Document Manager
.ix X11 version, Document Manager
.ix Terminal version, Document Manager
.ix Window, X11
The Document Manager has the same panels, keys and messages in the two versions.
What differs is the shell around them.
.table 9 51
Subject | Terminal version, then X11 version
Screen | The terminal, as large as it is (80 by 25 when the terminal reports no size);
 | a window of 80 columns and 50 rows.
Size | A resize of the terminal redraws the screen; the window of the X11
 | version follows a change of its height, and its width cannot be changed.
Keypad + | The plus key, or Alt-+; the keypad plus key.
Closing | The program is left by Quit; the close button of the window does
 | not end it.
Editor | Takes the terminal, and the screen of the menu is given up while it
 | runs; opens its own window, and the window of the Document Manager waits.
Viewer | Needs an X display ({c:DISPLAY}); opens its own window.
Colors | Those of the terminal; a dark background, bold in white and
 | dimmed text in grey.
.end

The environment variables that change the font and the size of the window of the
X11 version are in {n:appcmd} and {n:appx11}.  The key {k:Keypad +} of the
panels is the keypad plus key in the X11 version; a terminal that sends the
plus key as an ordinary plus makes the same list open, and so does {k:F2}
in both versions.
.note A resize of the terminal while the Editor or the Viewer runs is harmless:
  the menu is drawn again at the new size when the program is back.
